# Shell scripts MUST reach macOS with LF endings.
#
# A CRLF shebang fails as "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", which reads like a
# broken script rather than a line-ending problem and costs an hour to work out.
# core.autocrlf is a per-machine setting (it is `true` on the Windows box these
# are authored on), so without this the outcome depends on how each clone
# happens to be configured. Pin it instead.
*.command  text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf

# The Windows launcher is the mirror image: a .bat wants CRLF.
*.bat      text eol=crlf
